  annotation "note_1771590240891_1", anchor: "maintained by ☽'oon' Communion sympathizers who had been Touched long enough that their testimony cannot be cleanly separated from ice-memory contamination", text: "Every factual claim in this entry rests on a documentary foundation I have just told the reader is contaminated. The Midnight Claws sealed the records. The record-keepers were Touched. The oral tradition is tunnel-chant. The ice-memory at this depth is layered with corruption residue older than the colony. I have no clean source for any of this, and I proceeded anyway with declarative sentences. On a better day I would call that editorial pragmatism. Today I will call it what it is.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590240891_2", anchor: "Fire-core braziers installed before the breach remain active", text: "Fire-cores exhaust in months. These have been submerged for three generations. Either the witnesses are wrong about what they are seeing through those ice-windows, or something in the flooded passages is sustaining a thermal reaction that has no precedent in any fire-core literature I have catalogued — and I have catalogued all of it. The canon facts are explicit: fist-sized crystals, months of warmth, then nothing. Whatever is glowing down there is not operating under terms we understand.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771590240891_3", anchor: "approximately one full cycle of fuel for the Aurora Stack", text: "Pre-breach inventory estimates from a merchant guild that was already losing territory. Three generations of submersion in corruption-saturated water, and I am citing supply projections as though they were current assay reports. Recoverable reserves could be the full cycle. Could be zero. Publishing this figure in an era of quarter-cycle rationing is not scholarship. It is a provocation with a footnote.", type: :correction, display: :popout
